    <sys:String x:Key="RecoveryCenterTitle">Recovery Center</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RecoveryCenterDescription">Each tool solves a different problem. Read its effect before continuing; none silently removes daily time or application rules.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TrustCurrentClockTitle">Trust the current Windows clock</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TrustCurrentClockDescription">If Kvieta stopped the session after detecting a forward or backward clock jump, this clears the clock warning after you verify Windows date and time. It does not change the clock.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TrustCurrentClockRequirement">Requires: administrator PIN + Windows administrator approval. Use only when the clock is correct.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="TrustCurrentClockAction">Approve clock</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RestoreSettingsTitle">Restore the last verified settings copy</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RestoreSettingsDescription">Replaces the current settings file with Kvieta's last verified backup. Usage history is preserved; recent settings changes may be reverted.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RestoreSettingsRequirement">Requires: administrator PIN + Windows administrator approval. Use when settings are corrupt or look incorrect.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RestoreSettingsAction">Restore settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RepairInstallationTitle">Repair the Kvieta installation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RepairInstallationDescription">Windows Installer revalidates signed Kvieta files and the Guardian service installation. It does not delete your plan, PIN, history, or rules.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RepairInstallationRequirement">Requires: Kvieta installed by MSI + Windows administrator approval. Use for missing files or a stopped service.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RepairInstallationAction">Repair installation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RecoveryCenterPrivacyNote">Recovery audit stores only the action name, result, and time on this device; it never stores the PIN, recovery code, or private content.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="RecoveryCenterOpenFailed">Recovery Center could not be opened</sys:String>
